[Music]  the ninth episode of star trek picard's  second season boldly goes where no trek  show has been before bringing us a  rarely seen version of the enterprise  and a shockingly dark past for a  character we thought we knew  during flashbacks to the childhood of  jean-luc picard we see the future  captain of the enterprise sitting at the  table in his family home on the table  near him is a toy sure to make trekkies  eyes wide a model of the nx01 refit the  nx01 is easily identifiable as the  titular starship featured in the four  season series star trek enterprise which  premiered in 2001 and starred scott  bakula as captain jonathan archer but  the refit aspect is what makes this  model especially unique because this  version of the nx01 enterprise was never  seen on screen it has only been the  subject of conjecture developed by  designers and model makers for a future  the series never saw the design was  originally planned to be introduced in a  fifth season of enterprise that never  happened thanks to an abrupt  cancellation in 2005 and has only ever  been seen off-screen artwork of the nx01  refit was seen in the 2014 release of  the star trek ships of the line calendar  series while polar lights produced a  model kit to the variant starship as  well in fact the version we see in this  episode appears to be a model produced  by eagle moss as part of their hero  collection series of star trek starships  in episode 9 titled hide and seek we  finally learn the truth behind picard  and his mother's games of hide and seek  a reference to a moment in the ninth  star trek film star trek insurrection in  that movie commander data is  malfunctioning and on the run leaving it  up to picard and wharf to track him down  while on the shuttlecraft captain picard  notes that as a boy he and his mother  used to play games of hide and seek  which we've seen firsthand this season  come out come out wherever you are  however we now learn there was far more  to those games than we ever imagined  here we discovered that a fateful game  of hide and seek led to a terrible  incident to picard's youth it started  innocently enough with a game in the  chateau but after a short time picard's  mother asks him to continue the game in  the tunnels beneath the estate picard  remarks that the tunnels are forbidden  but she manages to coax him down there  in the hopes of leaving the chateau  entirely his mother takes him through  the dark tunnel attempting to run from  her husband but jean-luc gets stuck in a  wooden floorboard his mother leaves  without him and young picard must be  rescued by his father later that evening  his mother suffers a severe mental  breakdown and takes her online adding  dark new context to a seemingly innocent  moment in star trek insurrection  ever since season 1 of star trek picard  fans have wondered what the deal is with  this new improved 7-9 what happened on  her adventures following star trek  voyager that caused her to turn to  vigilantism and the fenris rangers  rather than starfleet well thanks to  episode 9 of picard season 2 we finally  know why she turned out the way she did  the answer harkens back to several  episodes of star trek voyager while  running from the newly minted borg  soldiers in the tunnels beneath the  picard chateau 7 of 9 and rafi have  another heart to heart as they arm up  and prepare to take on a squad of  soldiers chasing them rafi comments at  seven who is taking command of the  situation sounds a lot like a starship  captain she says that seven should have  joined starfleet and it's then that we  learned why she never did finally giving  fans a deeper glimpse into what happened  to seven after returning to the alpha  quadrant in the star trek voyager finale  according to seven she did attempt to  join starfleet but was turned away  because of her time as a board drone  apparently her former captain janeway  went to bad for her even threatening to  resign but seven opted to abandon her  academy aspirations and become a fenris  ranger this chain of events mirrors  concerns that seven of nine expressed  more than once since star trek voyager  when she considered staying behind in  the delta quadrant because she feared  that she would not be accepted on earth  it seems that her beliefs were  well-founded  one of the many unresolved questions  fans had about star trek voyager is what  became of the doctor's autonomous  holographic emitter a piece of 29th  century technology picked up during the  crew's time travel adventure in future's  end the device allows the doctor to  leave the confines of not just the  sickbay but the ship entirely and it  gives him a freedom of movement that  makes him more like a human than ever  before but how would starfleet feel  about using such an advanced piece of  tech seemingly in violation of the  temporal prime directive here we find  out and it seems that the doctor's  mobile emitter has become a piece of  invaluable technology found aboard the  la serena as she struggles with the  board queen while on board the ship  dratty is able to power up the vessel's  ech however this is not the emergency  command hologram first seen in the star  trek voyager episode tinker tenor dr spy  on an emergency combat hologram turns  out this ship can make a hologram from  anyone who's ever been on board  including an emergency combat hologram  this hologram which is in the image of  the crew's deadly romulan cohort elenor  sports what appears to be an updated  version of the mobile emitter which is  used to keep borg forces and the jaradi  queen at bay though we learn little  about the device holographic eleanor  points out that he exists separate from  the ship's systems to keep the lockout  codes out of the queen's reach elner  also suggests that not only is the 29th  century device lived on but may now be  in regular use throughout starfleet  since beginning of the season picard's  mother yvette has played a major role in  the story yvette is only seen once since  star trek the next generation when she  appears during the hallucination that  the captain experiences while traveling  through an unusual region of space in  the season one episode where no one has  gone before in that distant part of the  galaxy thoughts become reality and  picard finds himself face to face with  his mother in his hallucinatory vision  yvette picard asks her son to sit with  her for a cup of tea in a chat this  can't be  you've been  dead but i'm always with you  you know that  in this episode of picard we learn the  exact nature of that tragic death at  first this seems like an irreconcilable  retcon with yvette dying as a young  woman rather than the elderly version we  saw on star trek the next generation  even as a hallucination how could picard  remember her as an old woman if she  never was one but apparently the writers  thought about this picard says that long  after her death he often imagined her  having grown older and inviting him for  a cup of tea and chats as an old woman  it's a clever easter egg for longtime  fans that helps resolve a potential plot  hole in a satisfying way  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

